Id: cry001w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_crypto
Fix: Point rngd at the hardware RNG (rngd -r /dev/hwrng), or stop it.
References: rngd(8)
Controls: NIST SC-12, SC-13; ISO 8.24

The random-number daemon feeds from a software device: it goes
through the motions and adds no entropy. Point it at the
hardware RNG, or stop it where there is none.
